---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import InstallBar from '../components/InstallBar.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Quickstart"
	eyebrow="[ 02 · FIRST RUN ]"
	description="From zero to a SecurityReport against a Testnet Contract ID."
>
	<ol class="steps">
		<li>
			<strong>Install</strong>
			<InstallBar />
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Grab a Testnet Contract ID</strong>
			<p>
				Must match <code>C</code> + 55 base32 characters, e.g.
				<code>C…</code> from your own deploy or a fixture you are authorized to test.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Interactive TUI</strong>
			<pre><code>kuyfi</code></pre>
			<p>
				Menu: <code>[1] OSINT Scanner</code> → paste Contract ID → review attack surface
				→ <code>[2] Chaos Monkey</code> → export with <code>[J]</code> / <code>[P]</code> /
				<code>[B]</code>.
			</p>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Headless (CI / scripting)</strong>
			<pre><code>kuyfi CXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX --json --pdf</code></pre>
		</li>
	</ol>

	<Callout type="danger" title="Authorization required">
		<p>
			Chaos Monkey can submit <strong>real Testnet transactions</strong>. Only run against
			contracts you own or have written authorization to test. Unauthorized fuzzing may be
			illegal or against ToS.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2>Minimal mental model</h2>
	<pre><code>Contract ID
  → OSINT Scanner (read-only WASM / contractspecv0)
  → Chaos Monkey (type-aware vectors, simulate first)
  → classify DiagnosticEvent traces
  → SecurityReport → JSON / PDF</code></pre>

	<h2>What “success” looks like</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Scanner lists functions + UDTs without needing source.</li>
		<li>Chaos Monkey prints progress, then a findings summary (SECURE / PRECONDITION noise filtered).</li>
		<li>JSON/PDF share the same <code>reportId</code> and <code>schemaVersion: "1.0.0"</code>.</li>
		<li>Broadcast findings include stellar.expert Testnet links when a tx was sent.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Next</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Understand the <a href={withBase('/pipeline')}>pipeline</a></li>
		<li>Read <a href={withBase('/findings')}>finding semantics</a></li>
		<li>Wire agents via <a href={withBase('/for-llms')}>For LLMs</a></li>
	</ul>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
	.steps {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	.steps > li {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
	.steps strong {
		color: var(--text);
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
	}
</style>
